{
 "title": "Solving a Quadratic",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "The problem",
   "say": "We want the values of x that make x squared minus 5x plus 6 equal to zero.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "t1",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 40,
     "text": "Solving a Quadratic",
     "size": 56,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "id": "p1",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 140,
     "text": "x² − 5x + 6 = 0",
     "size": 48,
     "anchor": "middle",
     "color": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Try the formula",
   "say": "First, try the quadratic formula. Here a is 1, b is minus 5, and c is 6.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "f1",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 240,
     "text": "Try the formula:",
     "size": 36
    },
    {
     "id": "f2",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 300,
     "text": "x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) / 2a",
     "size": 40
    },
    {
     "id": "f3",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 380,
     "text": "a = 1, b = −5, c = 6",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "gray"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Plug in the numbers",
   "say": "Substituting gives 5 plus or minus the square root of 1, over 2, so x is 3 or 2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "f4",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 450,
     "text": "x = (5 ± √(25 − 24)) / 2",
     "size": 40
    },
    {
     "id": "f5",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 520,
     "text": "x = (5 ± 1) / 2",
     "size": 40
    },
    {
     "id": "f6",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 590,
     "text": "x = 3 or x = 2",
     "size": 40,
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Switch methods",
   "say": "That works, but it is a lot of work for this equation. Factoring is simpler, so let's switch.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "nb",
     "op": "rect",
     "x": 880,
     "y": 280,
     "w": 560,
     "h": 180,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "id": "n1",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 900,
     "y": 300,
     "text": "That works, but it's heavy.\nThere is a simpler way:\nfactoring!",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Find two numbers",
   "say": "Clear the board. We need two numbers that multiply to 6 and add to minus 5. Those are minus 2 and minus 3.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "e1",
     "op": "erase",
     "ids": [
      "f1",
      "f2",
      "f3",
      "f4",
      "f5",
      "f6",
      "n1",
      "nb"
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "g1",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 250,
     "text": "Find two numbers: product 6, sum −5",
     "size": 40,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "id": "g2",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 330,
     "text": "−2 and −3",
     "size": 44,
     "anchor": "middle",
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Factor and split",
   "say": "So the equation factors as x minus 2 times x minus 3. A product is zero only when one factor is zero.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "g3",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 430,
     "text": "(x − 2)(x − 3) = 0",
     "size": 48,
     "anchor": "middle",
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "id": "g4",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 530,
     "text": "x − 2 = 0   or   x − 3 = 0",
     "size": 40,
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Answer and check",
   "say": "So x equals 2 or x equals 3. Plugging each back in gives zero, so both work.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "id": "g5",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 620,
     "text": "x = 2   or   x = 3",
     "size": 48,
     "anchor": "middle",
     "color": "green",
     "underline": true
    },
    {
     "id": "g6",
     "op": "write",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 740,
     "text": "Check: 4 − 10 + 6 = 0 and 9 − 15 + 6 = 0",
     "size": 32,
     "anchor": "middle",
     "color": "gray"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}